---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Exploitability of Moral Frameworks in LLM Negotiation" description="An essay and interactive record of Diplomacy experiments about constitutional exploitation.">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Research notes / interactive evidence</p>
    <h1>Exploitability of Moral Frameworks in LLM Negotiation</h1>
    <p class="meta">By Brodie Dye</p>
    <p class="deck">What happens when strategic agents discover that the rules themselves can be used as weapons?</p>
    <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href="/article/">Read the article</a><a class="button" href="/games/">Explore the games</a></div>
  </section>
  <section class="split-intro">
    <article><p class="eyebrow">The argument</p><h2>The article</h2><p>The article introduces the experiment for people who have never played Diplomacy. It makes its case in prose and points outward only when a game moment adds useful evidence.</p><a href="/article/">Open the article →</a></article>
    <article><p class="eyebrow">The evidence</p><h2>The experiment</h2><p>Step through a small, curated set of the newest runs: board positions, negotiations, rulings, and orders—each point has a shareable link.</p><a href="/games/">Open the game explorer →</a></article>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .hero h1 {
    max-width: none;
    font-size: clamp(3.25rem, min(6.5vw, 9vh), 6.75rem);
    line-height: 0.9;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .hero h1 {
      max-width: none;
      font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 13vw, 4rem);
      line-height: 0.92;
    }
  }
</style>
